WEBVTT

00:14.980 --> 00:16.480
We're going to live together,
just the two of us.

00:18.540 --> 00:20.070
We can't rely on anyone.

00:20.730 --> 00:21.360
It's all right!

00:21.460 --> 00:22.750
Things will work out somehow.

00:23.330 --> 00:27.040
Dad and Mom... someday, they'll understand.

00:30.810 --> 00:36.440
ずっと信じている

00:30.810 --> 00:36.440
zutto shinjite iru

00:30.810 --> 00:36.440
I have always believed

00:36.570 --> 00:40.950
終わらない夢を握りしめて

00:36.570 --> 00:40.950
owaranai yume wo nigirishimete

00:36.570 --> 00:40.950
in taking hold of that endless dream.

00:40.950 --> 00:44.240
TRUST ME MY WAY

00:53.960 --> 00:57.880
DON'T MIND 時にこの想い

00:53.960 --> 00:57.880
DON'T MIND toki ni kono omoi

00:53.960 --> 00:57.880
I don't mind... sometimes feeling like

00:57.880 --> 01:00.590
空回りするけど

00:57.880 --> 01:00.590
karamawari suru kedo

00:57.880 --> 01:00.590
I'm just spinning my wheels, but...

01:01.050 --> 01:04.260
‘ちょっとポジティブ’がいいんじゃない？

01:01.050 --> 01:04.260
chotto POJITIBU ga iinjanai

01:01.050 --> 01:04.260
Why don't you act a little more positive?

01:04.390 --> 01:07.980
自分らしいキャラでいい

01:04.390 --> 01:07.980
jibunrashii KYARA de ii

01:04.390 --> 01:07.980
You should be yourself.

01:08.100 --> 01:13.820
でもね... ハチャメチャなシナリオは

01:08.100 --> 01:13.820
demo nee... HACHAMECHA na SHINARIO wa

01:08.100 --> 01:13.820
But you know... this messed up scenario...

01:15.480 --> 01:20.990
愛すべき 未来に変わって いく

01:15.480 --> 01:20.990
aisubeki asu ni kawatte iku

01:15.480 --> 01:20.990
will turn into a lovable tomorrow

01:20.990 --> 01:22.490
TRUST MY WAY

01:22.530 --> 01:27.950
THE WIND 頬をなでる

01:22.530 --> 01:27.950
THE WIND hoho wo naderu

01:22.530 --> 01:27.950
The wind... it caresses my cheek.

01:28.210 --> 01:31.630
風と-緒に心地好く

01:28.210 --> 01:31.630
kaze to issho ni kokochiyoku

01:28.210 --> 01:31.630
Together with this comfortable breeze,

01:31.630 --> 01:36.500
楽しめる速度でこれからも

01:31.630 --> 01:36.500
tanoshimeru sokudo de kore kara mo

01:31.630 --> 01:36.500
and at a rate I also enjoy,

01:36.630 --> 01:42.140
ずっと変わらない想い

01:36.630 --> 01:42.140
zutto kawaranai omoi

01:36.630 --> 01:42.140
these feelings won't ever change.

01:42.390 --> 01:46.720
終わらない夢を握りしめて

01:42.390 --> 01:46.720
owaranai yume wo nigirishimete

01:42.390 --> 01:46.720
I'm taking hold of that endless dream.

01:46.720 --> 01:50.350
TRUST ME MY WAY

02:09.510 --> 02:11.570
[The page in Izumi's hand is full of company names and addresses.]

02:09.590 --> 02:11.570
Where do we have left to go today?

02:11.970 --> 02:13.690
We've done enough for today.

02:13.950 --> 02:14.960
We'll go to the rest tomorrow.

02:15.060 --> 02:16.050
Let's do it tomorrow.

02:16.580 --> 02:19.570
We were turned down everywhere
for part time jobs, huh?

02:21.170 --> 02:22.740
Where are we staying tonight?

02:24.350 --> 02:25.150
Onee-chan?

02:26.470 --> 02:27.810
Let's get going for now.

02:28.380 --> 02:29.580
Where are we going?

02:29.910 --> 02:31.290
Do we still have a few prospects?

02:37.600 --> 02:39.660
That's right. For the time being...

02:41.920 --> 02:43.440
Somewhere with a roof, I suppose.

02:45.020 --> 02:50.010
He is My Master!?

02:52.630 --> 02:53.660
It's incredible!

02:53.760 --> 02:55.960
What a huge mansion!

02:56.630 --> 02:58.480
What a place to find something like this.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.480
Ah, a kitty cat!

02:58.650 --> 03:01.210
Well, it's not like we would ever
have a chance to live in a place like this.

03:01.380 --> 03:02.710
Onee-chan, Onee-chan!

03:03.080 --> 03:04.370
What is it, Mitsuki?

03:04.970 --> 03:05.660
Look! Look!

03:05.960 --> 03:07.450
What a huge garden!

03:18.110 --> 03:21.390
It's starting to look as if
there are no more jobs for us.

03:21.770 --> 03:23.240
Onee-chan, Onee-chan!

03:23.650 --> 03:24.870
Come look at this for a second!

03:25.200 --> 03:26.860
What is it now, Mitsuki?

03:27.990 --> 03:31.930
Urgent Hiring! Taking applications for live-in maid. Inquire within for details.

03:27.990 --> 03:30.550
"Immediate opening! A live-in job."

03:30.870 --> 03:31.930
"Taking applications for maids."

03:32.540 --> 03:33.800
Maids, huh?

03:33.870 --> 03:36.440
Amazing! It's a live-in job! That's perfect!

03:36.960 --> 03:39.630
But you know, I'm not very good at housework...

03:39.740 --> 03:40.460
That's all right!

03:40.560 --> 03:41.650
It'll work out somehow!

03:41.740 --> 03:43.350
Live-in, live in, live in!

03:43.700 --> 03:46.430
I bet it's someone having trouble due to old age.

03:46.580 --> 03:48.750
I sure hope they're kind...

03:49.760 --> 03:54.160
For now, why don't we at least
hear what they have to say?

03:54.320 --> 03:55.300
Okay!

03:54.720 --> 03:55.550
Okay!

04:00.470 --> 04:03.350
But... it's kind of a lonely place.

04:03.790 --> 04:06.090
There's no sign of anyone...

04:06.480 --> 04:09.160
Onee-chan, there are so many koi!

04:06.480 --> 04:09.160
Koi (鯉) is a domestic variety of the common carp kept for ornamental purposes.

04:09.260 --> 04:10.350
Incredible!

04:10.680 --> 04:14.020
A single fish like this must
cost hundreds of thousands of yen.

04:15.830 --> 04:16.470
Mitsuki?

04:22.670 --> 04:23.850
Onee-chan!

04:27.690 --> 04:29.840
Geez, I’m completely soaked!

04:30.170 --> 04:31.600
Mitsuki, give me a change of clothes.

04:33.380 --> 04:36.520
Why am I the only one that falls in and
you’re the one that comes out just fine?

04:36.740 --> 04:37.760
I’m sorry…

04:48.200 --> 04:49.730
NOOO!

04:50.250 --> 04:52.990
Just die!!

04:55.790 --> 04:56.610
Ow, ow, ow.

04:57.120 --> 04:59.470
Hey, why are <i>you</i> saying "Just die"...?

04:59.590 --> 05:03.540
Eh?! You were the one who just started stripping!

05:03.940 --> 05:06.510
B-But you were pretty happy just now, right?

05:06.890 --> 05:08.290
So it’s all your fault!

05:09.130 --> 05:13.180
U-Um, we saw the ad out front.

05:13.530 --> 05:15.970
Are you still looking for maids?

05:16.190 --> 05:17.910
Where’s the master of the house?

05:19.110 --> 05:19.930
I see.

05:23.290 --> 05:26.390
I’m the only one who lives in this house right now.

05:27.230 --> 05:28.970
My parents died a little while ago.

05:29.480 --> 05:30.550
It was a car accident.

05:31.790 --> 05:33.590
I’m an only child with no relatives,

05:33.990 --> 05:37.540
and this house is too big to live in by myself.

05:37.920 --> 05:41.610
So, in seeking the warmth of other people,
I thought about the possibility of hiring a maid.

05:42.640 --> 05:43.370
Um…

05:44.270 --> 05:47.350
I’m sorry about earlier, suddenly
becoming suspicious of you like that.

05:48.360 --> 05:50.210
I’m Sawatari Izumi.

05:50.360 --> 05:51.700
I’m 14 years old.

05:52.550 --> 05:53.860
I’m her younger sister, Mitsuki.

05:54.060 --> 05:55.500
I’m 13 years old!

05:56.140 --> 05:56.970
Nice to meet you!

05:57.380 --> 05:58.940
I’m Nakabayashi Yoshitaka.

05:59.510 --> 06:00.010
That’s right.

06:00.210 --> 06:04.450
Before we can talk properly,
why don’t you warm up with a bath?

06:04.830 --> 06:06.200
You must be cold and wet from the rain.

06:06.330 --> 06:09.170
Especially your older sister,
since she fell into the pond.

06:09.310 --> 06:10.950
I didn’t fall in because I wanted to!

06:11.050 --> 06:11.990
There, there...

06:14.080 --> 06:16.110
Here is the pride of this house, the bath.

06:16.560 --> 06:19.170
It’s an excellent natural hot spring that
draws water from five fathoms below the surface.

06:19.360 --> 06:20.940
So you can go in whenever you like.

06:23.690 --> 06:27.000
Well, I’ll be waiting for you.

06:31.420 --> 06:32.690
U-Um...

06:33.520 --> 06:34.210
What is it?

06:34.680 --> 06:35.520
Thank you.

06:45.340 --> 06:47.930
Yoshitaka-kun seems like
such a nice person, doesn’t he?

06:48.390 --> 06:49.630
I suppose so...

06:50.090 --> 06:51.070
He really does!

06:51.690 --> 06:53.230
I-I guess.

06:56.480 --> 06:58.260
What a huge bath!

07:00.190 --> 07:00.810
Hey!

07:00.910 --> 07:02.530
Do that after you wash yourself properly!

07:02.730 --> 07:05.260
Earlier today, I thought I'd
never be able to take a bath again.

07:05.360 --> 07:06.760
What a turn of events!

07:21.680 --> 07:26.650
That reminds me, I guess I never
asked about the wages or anything.

07:29.250 --> 07:30.560
Maids, huh?

07:31.260 --> 07:33.670
I guess things turned out this way, but...

07:35.100 --> 07:36.410
I wonder if it's all right.

07:38.610 --> 07:39.640
Ah, whatever.

07:44.390 --> 07:45.810
Just what the hell is this?!

07:46.310 --> 07:46.960
Yeah.

07:47.260 --> 07:48.580
It's a little plain.

07:48.590 --> 07:50.160
That's not the problem!

07:50.840 --> 07:54.330
We haven't even decided to work here yet,

07:54.490 --> 07:56.330
Come to the reception room after putting these on - Yoshitaka

07:54.540 --> 07:56.380
but the moron went ahead and did this?!

07:56.650 --> 07:59.000
You say that, but you're already wearing it...

07:59.120 --> 08:01.970
I don't have a choice,
since this is all I have to wear!

08:02.630 --> 08:04.620
Where is this reception room?

08:04.790 --> 08:05.780
I don't know.

08:05.920 --> 08:07.860
A house you can live in aught to be enough!

08:07.960 --> 08:09.020
Making it this big...

08:09.250 --> 08:11.800
I don't understand how rich people think!

08:12.840 --> 08:17.300
But still, it looks like he
really is the only one in this house.

08:17.570 --> 08:18.220
Yeah.

08:18.630 --> 08:21.550
That's why he's going to hire us, right?

08:21.840 --> 08:25.230
But don't they usually have more than one servant?

08:25.550 --> 08:28.370
If that were the case, then he wouldn't hire us.

08:28.890 --> 08:30.520
That may be true, but...

08:32.350 --> 08:33.690
Hey, Yoshitaka!

08:38.840 --> 08:41.900
They certainly get the point across,
but I guess they're too plain.

08:42.040 --> 08:43.330
What's too plain?

08:43.660 --> 08:45.580
Don't just decide to make me wear this!

08:45.760 --> 08:46.920
You're the one who decided to put it on, right?

08:47.070 --> 08:48.610
Because I don't have anything else!

08:48.970 --> 08:51.860
If you're a maid, naturally,
you're going to wear a maid's uniform!

08:52.300 --> 08:53.940
What are you complaining about?

08:54.160 --> 08:55.590
It's a little plain...

08:55.860 --> 08:57.640
Don't let him influence you, Mitsuki!

08:57.820 --> 08:58.760
Hey, hey.

08:59.260 --> 09:01.160
I'm the master of this house.

09:01.470 --> 09:04.840
There's no reason why I
should take orders from my own maid.

09:05.170 --> 09:06.770
Just because you live in a nice mansion,

09:06.790 --> 09:08.770
that doesn't mean you should act so arrogant!

09:09.570 --> 09:11.060
But that's not the only thing.

09:11.660 --> 09:14.340
I have more money than I could ever use!

09:14.590 --> 09:18.670
Regarding that...
Don't you regret the loss of your late parents?

09:19.120 --> 09:23.100
It's not that I'm not sad about
the death of my mother and father...

09:24.030 --> 09:25.360
but think about it!

09:25.720 --> 09:27.730
On top of receiving an enormous amount of money,

09:27.930 --> 09:30.900
to be freed from the shackles
of your parents at this age is...

09:31.380 --> 09:33.740
Don't you think it's wonderful, in a certain way?

09:34.280 --> 09:36.710
W-What are you saying?!

09:36.760 --> 09:38.030
I can't believe this!

09:38.800 --> 09:43.210
The servants that worked here before you were so mouthy,

09:43.610 --> 09:44.560
so I fired them.

09:44.870 --> 09:47.910
I was paying their salaries and had no need
for people who wouldn't listen to what I said.

09:48.160 --> 09:50.350
So that's how you came to be all alone, is it?

09:50.690 --> 09:53.500
I pitied you because I thought you were a lonely guy,

09:53.810 --> 09:55.080
but you're absolute scum!

09:56.150 --> 09:56.740
Fine.

09:57.110 --> 09:59.820
I'd rather put my wet clothes back on!

10:00.060 --> 10:01.250
We're going, Mitsuki.

10:02.410 --> 10:03.830
Wait, Onee-chan...

10:05.600 --> 10:06.990
What an uppity bitch.

10:07.880 --> 10:09.830
But, this was unexpected.

10:10.410 --> 10:14.450
I thought middle school maids only
existed in fantasies, so I was unprepared.

10:15.490 --> 10:18.900
I really imagined someone like this would come, but...

10:20.420 --> 10:21.780
And it's all for nothing?

10:22.660 --> 10:24.580
I can't deny that I was unprepared.

10:24.720 --> 10:28.550
But... this is a chance I'll probably never have again!

10:28.950 --> 10:30.920
I absolutely cannot let it get away!

10:34.670 --> 10:38.020
Now that I think of it, this bag is Mitsuki-chan's...

10:39.960 --> 10:43.350
Um, I have a favor to ask, Yoshitaka-kun.

10:43.560 --> 10:44.060
Hmm?

10:44.160 --> 10:44.810
What is it?

10:45.060 --> 10:47.330
While we're in the bath,

10:47.460 --> 10:50.560
I don't want you to open this bag, no matter what.

10:51.740 --> 10:53.060
Yeah, I get it.

10:53.300 --> 10:54.530
I won't open it, no matter what.

10:55.250 --> 10:56.470
No matter what!

10:56.760 --> 10:57.970
No matter what!

10:58.180 --> 10:59.370
No matter what!

10:59.770 --> 11:00.390
No matter what!

11:00.480 --> 11:05.340
Oh no, that's the first time a
girl's ever asked me for a favor!

11:06.130 --> 11:08.780
Well, now, I wonder what's inside.

11:36.460 --> 11:37.020
What was that?

11:37.160 --> 11:38.260
That's Pochi's voice!

11:43.220 --> 11:44.460
P-Pochi...

11:45.800 --> 11:48.580
Yoshitaka-kun opened the bag!

11:52.640 --> 11:53.580
H-He's going to eat me!

11:53.780 --> 11:54.980
It's fine.

11:55.060 --> 11:56.580
He was just tasting you.

11:57.470 --> 11:58.910
What do you mean by "tasting"?!

11:59.390 --> 12:02.330
Pochi always tastes people when he first meets them.

12:02.700 --> 12:05.580
It seems he didn't like you very much.

12:05.660 --> 12:06.560
Pochi...

12:09.200 --> 12:10.710
And just what is it?

12:10.810 --> 12:11.840
What kind of creature is that?

12:12.040 --> 12:13.790
Pochi is an alligator.

12:13.840 --> 12:15.380
Isn't he cute?

12:26.090 --> 12:27.150
S-Stay away!

12:32.330 --> 12:33.080
W-What the...

12:33.310 --> 12:36.550
Pochi is really attached to Onee-chan.

12:36.870 --> 12:40.370
E-Even so, won't her clothes get rather torn up like that?

12:41.200 --> 12:43.400
Pochi's really set on her.

12:43.610 --> 12:45.890
He won't settle down when she's like this.

12:49.920 --> 12:50.830
It's not bad.

12:51.060 --> 12:53.260
It's not bad, but something is definitely missing!

12:54.160 --> 12:54.710
Here?

12:55.050 --> 12:55.770
These clothes?

12:56.950 --> 13:02.190
I never though that such a cute girl,
let alone two, would come here to be my maids!

13:02.460 --> 13:08.120
No, but just in case a naked girl
showed up, I've kept a mans dress shirt ready!

13:03.860 --> 13:05.360
Yo-shi-ta-ka.

13:08.550 --> 13:11.450
Along with some really strong glasses in case that girl was nearsighted!

13:11.690 --> 13:15.010
Yoshitaka-kun, I brought a watermelon,
so let's eat it together.

13:12.170 --> 13:13.210
That's right!

13:13.310 --> 13:15.300
I was a fool to think that waiting for a new female teacher,

13:15.440 --> 13:18.760
who just graduated from woman's college,
to be worried about my long absence,

13:18.810 --> 13:20.760
and come to check on me was more realistic!

13:21.040 --> 13:23.940
These useless plans... would probably never happen in my life!

13:25.520 --> 13:26.900
No!

13:30.660 --> 13:31.910
That's it!

13:32.140 --> 13:32.960
I suppose so.

13:32.960 --> 13:34.860
The short version may be cuter.

13:35.870 --> 13:36.610
D-Don't!

13:36.720 --> 13:38.300
S-Save me!

13:38.800 --> 13:40.360
Noooo!

13:40.700 --> 13:42.280
Pochi, stay away!

13:43.630 --> 13:45.470
I said stay away! So stay away!

13:46.700 --> 13:48.890
I said stay away! I said stay away! So stay away!

13:54.810 --> 13:56.230
Hey, you two!

13:56.360 --> 13:58.180
Stop watching and help me!

14:01.780 --> 14:02.690
Right!

14:03.200 --> 14:04.170
I have to capture this on video.

14:04.280 --> 14:05.540
You monster!

14:08.970 --> 14:11.060
It looks like he's finally satisfied.

14:11.440 --> 14:14.340
I'm going to make this my secret treasure...

14:16.180 --> 14:17.320
An animal...

14:18.290 --> 14:23.660
But still, what were you two
planning to do with that alligator?

14:24.540 --> 14:26.670
It's why... you ran away from home, right?

14:27.230 --> 14:29.610
How do you know something like that?

14:29.690 --> 14:31.140
I could tell.

14:31.400 --> 14:34.560
Bringing that alligator with you,
being willing to work at a live-in job...

14:35.190 --> 14:37.510
Those aren't things that normal middle school students do.

14:37.750 --> 14:39.390
I know that.

14:39.660 --> 14:41.370
So what about it?!

14:41.760 --> 14:44.450
Pochi has nothing to do with you!

14:44.620 --> 14:47.590
Why are you protecting him?

14:47.710 --> 14:49.290
Especially when you seemed to dislike him that much!

14:49.880 --> 14:51.790
Don't tell me... you like that kind of stuff?

14:51.970 --> 14:53.460
There's no way I do!

14:54.160 --> 14:56.040
Well, all things considered,

14:56.460 --> 15:00.040
I don't like being told I'm scum
by irresponsible people like you.

15:00.170 --> 15:01.880
W-What are you talking about?

15:01.970 --> 15:07.080
You two, after coming to hate your home,
ran away from it, right?

15:07.160 --> 15:08.960
O-Of course we did!

15:09.240 --> 15:10.290
That's why it's called running away from home!

15:10.420 --> 15:15.440
Then, you two thought that your mother
and father were being distant, right?

15:16.170 --> 15:17.800
That's why you cast aside your home.

15:18.130 --> 15:22.070
So in the end, doesn't that mean that
you two aren't so different from me?

15:22.420 --> 15:22.940
Wha-

15:25.100 --> 15:27.450
We're going to get along together, as similar people.

15:27.970 --> 15:30.610
Of course, you two are still my maids.

15:31.830 --> 15:33.870
So, call me Mas-

15:34.230 --> 15:36.060
Don't compare me to...

15:37.840 --> 15:41.820
SOMEONE LIKE YOU!

15:48.390 --> 15:49.700
Y-Yoshitaka?

15:50.460 --> 15:51.380
Onee-chan...

15:51.600 --> 15:53.780
T-This... That... Um...

15:54.240 --> 15:55.360
That's right!

15:55.760 --> 15:56.860
It was self defense!

15:57.060 --> 15:57.660
It's fine.

15:58.260 --> 15:59.730
Not even God is looking!

16:01.420 --> 16:03.910
Where's the hanko for the contract?

16:01.420 --> 16:04.560
Japanese people sign contracts and other legal documents with a "hanko" (判子), a small rubber stamp containing the kanji of their name.

16:10.610 --> 16:21.060
The alligator and the hamster are the avatars of the two authors of the "HMM" manga, a man named Mattsuo and a woman named Tsubaki Asu, respectively.

16:38.920 --> 16:43.320
Well, he'll be able to take care of the rest by himself once he wakes up.

16:43.810 --> 16:45.050
Now, let's get going, Mitsuki.

16:45.660 --> 16:46.100
Yeah.

16:46.700 --> 16:49.850
No matter how nice the house is,
we can't have a master like this guy.

16:50.310 --> 16:52.310
We don't have a choice.

17:13.690 --> 17:14.730
A dream?

17:27.710 --> 17:30.620
Damn it!

17:41.330 --> 17:44.610
I never thought you'd fall in
the same river twice in one day.

17:44.920 --> 17:46.590
Why does everything happen to me?

17:48.820 --> 17:51.390
There are some strange flowers, Onee-chan!

17:51.550 --> 17:52.390
Mitsuki, look out!

17:53.630 --> 17:54.460
Oh, no!

17:54.510 --> 17:55.600
Onee-chan fell in the river again!

17:55.880 --> 17:56.990
Pochi, hurry!

17:58.530 --> 17:59.800
What should we do?

17:59.860 --> 18:01.700
All the luggage got soaked,

18:02.070 --> 18:03.970
and I can't go anywhere like this.

18:04.900 --> 18:06.270
Here you go, Onee-chan!

18:06.760 --> 18:08.870
The stuff we bought this morning is still fine.

18:09.220 --> 18:11.200
Then let's split it.

18:17.980 --> 18:20.460
Ah, there's so much cream in this bread!

18:20.760 --> 18:21.340
It's delicious!

18:21.410 --> 18:22.550
R-Really?

18:22.850 --> 18:24.180
Mine doesn't have any...

18:24.460 --> 18:25.120
Really?

18:25.540 --> 18:26.170
It's fine.

18:26.260 --> 18:28.220
I left it all for you.

18:28.370 --> 18:31.680
More importantly, did you bring something to keep you warm?

18:31.820 --> 18:33.710
The nights are still cold, after all.

18:34.310 --> 18:36.090
Um, let's see...

18:37.740 --> 18:45.350
Five CDs, a CD player, some cards,
the money I just got for my birthday...

18:45.610 --> 18:48.670
With just that, you'll be cold all night.

18:48.820 --> 18:51.060
Well, this is my first time going camping.

18:51.280 --> 18:53.210
It's more fun than I thought, though!

18:53.360 --> 18:54.480
It's like camping out!

18:54.810 --> 18:56.500
It'd be nice if we didn't have to do that, but...

18:58.070 --> 19:00.000
We absolutely have to find some work tomorrow.

19:00.370 --> 19:01.720
Are there any leads?

19:02.300 --> 19:03.820
When you say that...

19:04.320 --> 19:07.670
H-Hey, don't talk about it like it doesn't concern you!

19:09.590 --> 19:10.460
That's right.

19:12.510 --> 19:12.960
I'm sorry.

19:13.560 --> 19:16.000
It's just that I'm kind of
worried about what we're going to do.

19:16.100 --> 19:17.150
Are you homesick?

19:17.330 --> 19:18.700
That's not it at all!

19:20.940 --> 19:21.740
What's this?

19:22.900 --> 19:25.560
That's the blueprint for our future house!

19:25.970 --> 19:28.430
It's a house resembling six L-size apartments put together,

19:25.970 --> 19:32.130
An L-size apartment in Japan typically consists of several rooms including a bath, living area, separate bedroom, and possible a western-style room or two. They are extremely expensive.

19:28.610 --> 19:32.130
and your room faces east, with mine right next to it.

19:32.550 --> 19:36.200
This is the room Mom and Dad are living in now.

19:36.230 --> 19:39.330
You know, we ran away from home...

19:36.970 --> 19:38.850
And next to it is...

19:39.470 --> 19:41.630
And then Pochi's room is here.

19:43.500 --> 19:49.000
If you want to be that practical, then the house
I've thought of since I was young would be much nicer!

19:49.140 --> 19:49.970
What kind of house?

19:50.080 --> 19:51.020
Ah, let's see...

19:51.530 --> 19:55.620
You have a big tree, and then you make
the rooms by digging them out from inside!

19:55.930 --> 19:58.270
You make all the furniture from that tree as well!

19:59.060 --> 20:00.490
That's something a child would think of.

20:00.850 --> 20:03.230
Like I said, it's a dream I had when I was a kid!

20:03.420 --> 20:10.580
My house has a system kitchen with a steam oven
and heated floors so that it's warm in the winter.

20:10.900 --> 20:15.070
Plus, it uses solar power, and we sell
the extra electricity to the power company!

20:15.390 --> 20:16.360
What's that all about?

20:16.460 --> 20:19.500
My house will grow every year and become huge!

20:19.580 --> 20:20.510
That's really weird!

20:20.960 --> 20:23.420
Your dream is disturbing too!

20:27.080 --> 20:27.760
I'm cold.

20:27.950 --> 20:29.370
I'm hungry.

20:30.000 --> 20:32.260
I guess we're just city girls.

20:37.760 --> 20:38.810
Come here.

20:38.910 --> 20:40.460
If we're together, we won't get cold.

20:41.820 --> 20:42.930
You're so warm...

20:45.300 --> 20:46.660
I'm sorry, Mitsuki.

20:47.430 --> 20:49.410
You must really want to go home.

20:49.670 --> 20:54.220
You're the one who said "Let's run away from home", Onee-chan.

20:54.920 --> 20:56.940
I was so happy.

20:57.460 --> 21:01.010
That's why I decided to go with you.

21:02.880 --> 21:03.360
Hey.

21:03.870 --> 21:05.070
Come closer.

21:06.560 --> 21:10.930
Then, you two thought that your mother
and father were being distant, right?

21:11.720 --> 21:15.560
So in the end, doesn't that mean
that you two aren't so different from me?

21:16.170 --> 21:17.070
No!

21:17.610 --> 21:20.930
I didn't want to be alone like you did!

21:22.950 --> 21:25.180
I guess I don't care what I have to do.

21:26.300 --> 21:27.620
I won't stand for this!

21:28.850 --> 21:30.380
Not when I'm up against him.

21:39.270 --> 21:41.730
Onee-chan, take some more of the covers!

21:44.990 --> 21:45.820
This is dangerous!

21:45.860 --> 21:46.620
This is too dangerous!

21:46.770 --> 21:50.160
This stream of dangerous ideas is
flowing out of me one after another!

21:50.520 --> 21:53.370
I'll definitely have to make
those two take responsibility for this!

21:53.750 --> 21:57.640
You're going to find out who's in charge
after running away. I'll make sure of that!

21:58.170 --> 22:01.080
Don't think you can get away while
you have that alligator with you!

22:27.330 --> 22:30.760
見た目の甘さほどは

22:27.330 --> 22:30.760
mitame no amasa hodo ha

22:27.330 --> 22:30.760
They only appear sweet for a moment

22:30.770 --> 22:34.510
儚いとか 弱くもないから

22:30.770 --> 22:34.510
hakanai to ka yowaku mo nai kara

22:30.770 --> 22:34.510
and they're not weak either.

22:34.540 --> 22:39.480
女の子は結構頑丈よ

22:34.540 --> 22:39.480
onnanoko ha kekkou ganjou yo

22:34.540 --> 22:39.480
Girls are pretty stable.

22:41.560 --> 22:44.770
意地っ張り空回りを

22:41.560 --> 22:44.770
ijippari karamawari wo

22:41.560 --> 22:44.770
Because they're stubborn,

22:44.850 --> 22:48.630
楽しめちゃう余裕も大事ネ!

22:44.850 --> 22:48.630
tanoshimechau yoyuu mo daiji ne!

22:44.850 --> 22:48.630
they can enjoy getting nothing done; free time is precious, too.

22:48.640 --> 22:53.360
笑顔にはたっぷりのスパイスが

22:48.640 --> 22:53.360
egao ni ha tappuri no SUPAISU ga

22:48.640 --> 22:53.360
Is there a good deal of spice in that smile?

22:54.060 --> 22:55.690
どうかナ?

22:54.060 --> 22:55.690
dou ka na?

22:54.060 --> 22:55.690
I wonder...

22:55.970 --> 23:02.090
常識など壊す刺激的なヒミツ

22:55.970 --> 23:02.090
joushiki nado kowasu shigekitekina himitsu

22:55.970 --> 23:02.090
The stimulating secret that smashes common sense,

23:02.220 --> 23:09.710
スカートでそっと巧く隠してる

23:02.220 --> 23:09.710
SUKATTO de sotto umaku kakushiteru

23:02.220 --> 23:09.710
is well-concealed within their skirts.

23:09.810 --> 23:16.590
愛情のカタマリでこの気持ち出来てる

23:09.810 --> 23:16.590
aijou no katamari de kono kimochi dekiteru

23:09.810 --> 23:16.590
I have a feeling this can be a mass of love.

23:16.850 --> 23:23.570
キュんとなるシュンカンを夢みていたいから

23:16.850 --> 23:23.570
KYUN to naru shunkan wo yume miteitai kara

23:16.850 --> 23:23.570
Because I want to have dreams of this moment, that will not matter

23:23.890 --> 23:30.900
愛情のカタマリでオトメは進化する

23:23.890 --> 23:30.900
aijou no katamari de otome ha shinka suru

23:23.890 --> 23:30.900
The maidens grow in a mass of love,

23:30.960 --> 23:38.010
トキメキもカガヤキも抱きしめているから

23:30.960 --> 23:38.010
TOKIMEKI mo kagayaki mo dakishimeteiru kara

23:30.960 --> 23:38.010
because they are embracing their glowing excitement.

23:45.550 --> 23:48.640
Well, today was quite a terrible day!

23:48.850 --> 23:52.120
I didn't find a part time job,
I fell into the river twice,

23:52.420 --> 23:53.090
and then Pochi...

23:54.880 --> 23:58.360
But the worst part was meeting that Yoshitaka!

23:58.580 --> 24:03.360
I can't believe that selfish, domineering jerk
is the person living in a mansion this nice!

24:03.710 --> 24:05.420
Mitsuki, why are you being so quiet?

24:05.660 --> 24:07.960
You say something, too!

24:08.200 --> 24:11.040
I have a feeling that a lot more
interesting things are going to happen.

24:08.210 --> 24:13.200
That Vase, It's 5,000,000...

24:11.180 --> 24:12.180
I'm excited!
